{"step_index":5138,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T07:57:48Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-25T07:57:48Z\nCompleted At: 2026-09-25T07:57:48Z\nFile Path: `file:///home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/REPORTS/AUTONOMOUS_POLICY_CONTROLLED_AUDIT_AND_DESIGN.md`\nTotal Lines: 219\nTotal Bytes: 13944\nShowing lines 1 to 219\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # AUTONOMOUS-SAFE & POLICY-CONTROLLED ARCHITECTURE FORENSIC AUDIT & DESIGN REPORT\n2: \n3: Location: `/home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/REPORTS/AUTONOMOUS_POLICY_CONTROLLED_AUDIT_AND_DESIGN.md`  \n4: Date: 25 September 2026  \n5: Auditor: AGY Principal Master Agent  \n6: Target Environment: Azure Cloud Linux VM (Debian 12 x86_64)  \n7: Antigravity Version: `1.2.10`\n8: \n9: ---\n10: \n11: ## 1. OPERATIONAL PHILOSOPHY: APPROVAL-LESS BUT POLICY-CONTROLLED\n12: \n13: > 🛑 **CORE ARCHITECTURAL REALIZATION** 🛑\n14: >\n15: > The user's requirement is **NOT \"permission-less\"**, but **\"approval-less but policy-controlled\"**.\n16: > - The agent must NEVER halt mid-task to ask: *\"Can I run this command?\"* (Zero interactive prompts).\n17: > - Instead, the backend Policy Gateway silently and strictly verifies:\n18: >   `Agent + Project + Tool + Target + Operation → Is this valid under machine policy?`\n19: > - If valid → **ALLOW** (executed seamlessly by `--dangerously-skip-permissions`).\n20: > - If invalid, unsafe, or destructive → **DENY** (hard-blocked at `PreToolUse`).\n21: > - The Antigravity `PreToolUse` hook is an **Application-Level Tool Execution Enforcement Layer**, NOT an OS-level security boundary.\n22: \n23: ---\n24: \n25: ## 2. FORENSIC VERIFICATION OF 14 AUDIT ITEMS (ACTUAL EVIDENCE)\n26: \n27: ### 1. `--dangerously-skip-permissions` Actual Runtime Behavior\n28: - **Evidence:** `init_agy_sessions.sh` launches all agents with `$AGY_BIN --dangerously-skip-permissions`.\n29: - **Mechanism:** Suppresses Antigravity's interactive confirmation modals, setting native permi\n<truncated 11391 bytes>\n90:   - YouTube: Section 6 (Veo 3.1, SQLite truth, No FFmpeg) to `/home/azureuser/.openclaw/workspace/IROSCRIPT-CEO/social-media/youtube/AGENTS.md` (~80 lines).\n191:   - Telegram: Rule 14 (MTProto live search) to `/home/azureuser/telegram-bot/AGENTS.md` (~25 lines).\n192:   - Digital History: Rule 8 (OpenRecall protection) to `/home/azureuser/.openclaw/workspace/IROSCRIPT-CEO/PERSONAL AI AGENT/AGENTS.md` (~15 lines).\n193: - *Reversibility:* Instant restore from git.\n194: \n195: ### Step 2: Physical Workspace Decoupling\n196: - Decouple `/home/azureuser/Reporting-Agent` from `/home/azureuser/Ask-And-Research`.\n197: - Set up independent workspace directories.\n198: - *Reversibility:* Symlink can be restored instantly.\n199: \n200: ### Step 3: Standalone Fail-Closed Policy Gateway Development & Offline Test\n201: - Develop `/home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/POLICIES/policy_gateway.py`.\n202: - Enforce:\n203:   - Fail-Closed on all exceptions, timeouts, and unknown inputs.\n204:   - Self-protection (blocks edits to `hooks.json` and gateway scripts).\n205:   - Hard-blocks `sudo`, `docker`, `rm -rf`, `DROP TABLE`, `git push`, `git reset --hard`.\n206:   - Binary `allow` / `deny` only.\n207: - Run complete offline unit test suite before touching `hooks.json`.\n208: - *Reversibility:* Standalone script does not impact production until registered.\n209: \n210: ### Step 4: Hook Registration & Verification\n211: - Register `policy_gateway.py` in `/home/azureuser/.gemini/config/hooks.json` under `PreToolUse`.\n212: - Verify with live test tool calls.\n213: - *Reversibility:* Remove single JSON entry from `hooks.json`.\n214: \n215: ### Step 5: Concurrency Control & Independent Verification Pipeline\n216: - Deploy atomic file locker (`fcntl.flock`) and version schema in `AGY-MASTER/TASKS/`.\n217: - Wire Watchdog to emit structured `INCIDENT` JSONs with deduplication hash.\n218: - Enforce 3-tier verification: Action tests → Reporting health check → Master acceptance.\n219: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
